<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68774" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορόεις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, epith. of ear-rings, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρματα . . τρίγληνα μορόεντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.183
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.298
			</span></i>; expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				976.40
			</span></i>, as <i>wrought with much pains</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορέω</span>), in which sense it is used of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεύχη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.152
			</span></i>; by <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθάνατα, μόρου μὴ
			μετέχοντα</span>; perh. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόρον</span>, <i>clustering like mulberries.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόρος</span>) <i>fatal, deadly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					130
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				136
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μορόεντος ἐλαίης</span>, dub.
			sens., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Al.</u>
				455
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
